comments.body:
Answering the two questions above:

@Yaka88 — no PR: this repo doesn't accept external pull requests, so the fix lived on our fork branch ([fix/3572-antigravity-thought-signature](https://github.com/skygunner/magpie/tree/fix/3572-antigravity-thought-signature), `ba8d930`), for the maintainer to pick the way most fixes in this thread's history have landed.

@ericcug — your measurement was right for the tree you tested. Since yesterday this whole path has been reworked upstream in `2260390a0` ("a Gemini thought signature goes back only to the provider that gave it"): the refusal matcher now reads both "invalid" and "corrupted thought signature", and the ask-again-without-signatures retry reaches the native Gemini Developer API route, Code Assist (Antigravity) and Vertex AI — so both the switch-from-Vertex face this issue reported and the google face you measured are covered on current main (its tests include a corrupted-signature retry through AI Studio). Our fork branch is superseded by that and withdrawn.

The sigstore-scoping part of your last paragraph is what `2260390a0` now does as well: a signature is replayed only to the provider that gave it.

